cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this data, please cite it as below, credit "Daily Life Hacks", and
  link back to the study page the numbers came from or to
  https://www.daily-life-hacks.com/data/ so your readers can check the
  methodology. The original Daily Life Hacks selection, arrangement,
  calculations, field descriptions, and explanatory material are licensed
  under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International. Upstream facts and
  third-party material keep their own status and terms. Full scope:
  https://www.daily-life-hacks.com/data-reuse/
title: Daily Life Hacks Food Value Data
type: dataset
version: "2026.1"
date-released: "2026-07-26"
abstract: >-
  Twenty-two datasets (474 rows) of US grocery prices paired with USDA nutrient
  values, covering fiber per dollar, protein per dollar, protein quality
  adjusted with DIAAS, daily menu costing, and category-level rankings across
  produce, grains, legumes, dairy, meat, pantry staples and fast food. Nutrient
  values come from USDA FoodData Central. Prices are US national figures: BLS
  Average Price data where the item is tracked, Walmart national listings
  otherwise, observed July 2026. Every ranking is calculated as-purchased, with
  USDA refuse percentages removed so peels, pits and bone are not counted as
  food. The original Daily Life Hacks contribution is licensed under Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International. Source facts and third-party material
  aren't relicensed. Full scope is published at
  https://www.daily-life-hacks.com/data-reuse/
license: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
